diff --git a/saas/README.md b/saas/README.md
index 28b0891..de0a2ff 100644
--- a/saas/README.md
+++ b/saas/README.md
@@ -105,3 +105,58 @@ knife ssh 'hostname:fizzy-lb-*' 'sudo docker exec fizzy-load-balancer kamal-prox
 ## License
 
 fizzy-saas is released under the [O'Saasy License](LICENSE.md).
+
+## Hosted billing
+
+Hosted billing uses Stripe Checkout and the Stripe customer portal. Self-hosted
+installs have no billing or card quotas.
+
+| Plan | Monthly price (USD) | Published cards | Storage |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Free | $0 | 1,000 | 1 GB |
+| Unlimited | $20 | Unlimited | 5 GB |
+| Unlimited+ | $25 | Unlimited | 500 GB |
+
+Before enabling billing in a deployment:
+
+1. Run the SaaS database migrations (`bin/rails db:migrate:saas`).
+2. Create recurring monthly USD prices in Stripe for $20 and $25. Configure
+   `STRIPE_UNLIMITED_PRICE_ID` and `STRIPE_UNLIMITED_PLUS_PRICE_ID` with their IDs.
+3. Configure `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY` and `STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET` (the endpoint signing
+   secret, not the API key). Keep all secrets out of source control.
+4. Register the untenanted endpoint `/stripe/webhooks` for
+   `customer.subscription.created`, `customer.subscription.updated`, and
+   `customer.subscription.deleted`. Requests must have a valid Stripe signature.
+5. Enable the Stripe customer portal, including cancellation and changes between
+   the two approved monthly prices. Do not allow arbitrary quantities.
+
+Only account admins can initiate checkout or open the portal. Returning from
+checkout does not grant an allowance: a signed subscription webhook does. Webhook
+processing retrieves the current subscription from Stripe, so duplicate and
+out-of-order event payloads cannot replay old plan data. Stripe failures return
+an error so Stripe retries delivery. Active and trialing subscriptions grant the
+paid plan's allowance; canceled and non-active subscriptions fall back to Free.
+A scheduled cancellation retains its allowance until the subscription ends.
+
+The card quota counts published cards, including closed cards, not drafts or the
+account's card-number sequence. The last 100 cards show a countdown. At the limit,
+drafts can still be saved and edited, but publishing and JSON creation return 403.
+
+Staff can open `/admin/accounts` (also linked from admin statistics). Comp grants
+Unlimited without a payment; Uncomp removes that waiver without canceling an
+existing paid subscription. Usage overrides replace measured card count and/or
+bytes used; blank fields use measured usage and Reset deletes the override.
+Existing explicit storage exceptions are preserved and take precedence over a
+plan's storage allowance.
+
+Offline billing regression tests (all Stripe requests are stubbed):
+
+```sh
+DATABASE_ADAPTER=sqlite PARALLEL_WORKERS=1 bin/rails test \
+  saas/test/models/account saas/test/controllers/account \
+  saas/test/controllers/card saas/test/controllers/admin \
+  saas/test/controllers/stripe
+```
+
+A live Stripe checkout, portal, and webhook smoke test is still required before
+production rollout using the deployment's actual prices and credentials.
diff --git a/saas/app/controllers/account/billing/checkouts_controller.rb b/saas/app/controllers/account/billing/checkouts_controller.rb
